pstack for Muse: unofficial adaptation
=====================================

This repo is a modified copy of pstack by Lauren Tan, taken from the
cursor/plugins repository:

  Source:   https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack
  Commit:   6b0300214a09fd6029cfb7077043125758cd1fd2 (pstack version 0.15.36)
  License:  MIT, see LICENSE (kept verbatim, Copyright (c) 2026 Lauren Tan)

It is not an official release and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the
pstack author or Cursor. All credit for pstack goes to its author, Lauren Tan
(@poteto, https://github.com/poteto). Nothing of hers was rebranded: this is
"pstack, adapted for Muse", not a new work.

Changes from upstream pstack/ (everything not listed here is the author's
work, adapted only where the tooling differs):

  1. Every skill, playbook, principle, guide page, agent, and automation
     was adapted from Cursor / Claude Code tooling to Muse tooling. The
     methodology is unchanged: go deep first, smallest verifiable units,
     test-first where cheap, prove it works, delete before adding.
     See PORTING-NOTES.md for the full Cursor-to-Muse mapping and for
     anything deliberately left Cursor-specific.
  2. Each skill gained a skill.yaml (Muse skill metadata: name, title,
     description, category), matching the format Muse reads for
     custom skills. The SKILL.md files keep their upstream frontmatter
     where it still applies; Cursor-only frontmatter keys
     (disable-model-invocation, icon, color, is_background) were dropped.
  3. plugin.json at this root is adapted: name "pstack-muse", version
     0.15.36, author Lauren Tan, license MIT. The "$schema" key was
     removed; the manifest is informational, not schema-conformant.
  4. .cursor-plugin/ was removed (Cursor-specific manifest). The upstream
     manifest is at https://github.com/cursor/plugins/blob/main/pstack/.cursor-plugin/plugin.json.
  5. docs/harness/claude-code.md (the Claude Code adapter) was replaced
     by docs/harness/muse.md (the Muse adapter). The Claude adapter is
     unchanged upstream at https://github.com/cursor/plugins/blob/main/pstack/docs/harness/claude-code.md.
  6. Added this NOTICE file, PORTING-NOTES.md, and a replacement README.md.
     The upstream README is at https://github.com/cursor/plugins/blob/main/pstack/README.md.

Model routing: upstream pstack picks a model per role (code delegates to
Grok, judgment to Opus 5.5) and /setup-pstack writes those choices to a
Cursor rule. Muse runs one model, so there is no per-role model choice
here. /setup-pstack in this port configures effort and fan-out preferences
instead, and every delegate is a Muse subagent of the same model. The
multi-model review panels become same-model independent runs; agreement
between two independent runs is still high signal.

What does not work in Muse (marked in place, not silently dropped):

  - Cursor Automations and the /automate built-in (benny pack): the
    triage / reproduce-and-fix skills are kept as manual skills, but
    there is no automation runtime for them in Muse.
  - Bugbot and the agentic security review (Cursor-only): the skeptical
    review posture is kept; the Bugbot-specific steps are marked N/A.
  - /loop, Custom Modes, and Cursor's built-in /create-skill: no Muse
    equivalent; the ported text says so where it comes up.
  - deslop, control-cli, control-ui: these ship in cursor-team-kit, which
    is not ported here.
